stress resilience, weather assessment (technical), computer skills. Concerns: weak memory for numbers (attention), nasty remarks (crew cooperation, communication). So mixed.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality), difficulty communicating ideas (communication), regarded as egocentric (crew cooperation), not willing to further education (adaptability), keeps calm in crisis (stress resilience), understands complicated technology (technical). Strengths: decision speed, calm, technical. Concerns: communication, egocentric, not willing to learn.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical/decision), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), regarded as know-it-all (crew cooperation), has a hot temper (stress/cooperation). Strengths: concentration, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: know-it-all, hot temper.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely B has strong reliability and stress but poor teamwork. C has many strengths but poor communication. D has responsibility and problem solving but hot temper. A has anticipation and leadership but not open to ideas.\n\nWhich candidate balances? Maybe Candidate B: conscientious, handles stress, good weather assessment, but nasty remarks is serious for crew cooperation. Could be mitigated? Not sure.\n\nCandidate C: calm, quick decisions, technical, but egocentric and communication issues.\n\nCandidate D: responsibility, concentration, problem solving, but hot temper and know-it-all.\n\nProbably the best overall is Candidate B? But nasty remarks could be disqualifying. Maybe Candidate D's hot temper is also serious. Candidate A's not open to new ideas may affect adaptability.\n\nWe need to start discussion, maybe propose Candidate B as provisional recommendation, citing strengths and acknowledging concerns, and ask for others' input on crew cooperation concerns.\n\nThus public message: propose B, mention strengths (conscientious, stress handling, weather assessment) and concerns (nasty remarks). Suggest need to verify cooperation.\n\nProceed."}
